---
source: system/tests/help.rs
expression: "help_output(\"renice\")"
---
Alter priority of running processes

Usage: renice [-n|--priority|--relative] priority [-p|--pid] pid...
       renice [-n|--priority|--relative] priority -g|--pgrp pgid...
       renice [-n|--priority|--relative] priority -u|--user user...

Arguments:
  <ARGS>...  Priority value and targets

Options:
  -n, --priority <PRIORITY_FLAG>  Specify the scheduling priority (absolute by default)
      --relative                  Use relative priority adjustment instead of absolute
  -p, --pid                       Interpret targets as process IDs (default)
  -g, --pgrp                      Interpret targets as process group IDs
  -u, --user                      Interpret targets as usernames or UIDs
  -h, --help                      Print help
